---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import tools from '../data/tools.json';import filings from '../data/filings.json';import {site} from '../site.config';const snapshotDate=String(filings.asOf).slice(0,10);import {feeDrag} from '../lib/calc';const d=feeDrag({initial:10000,contribution:0,years:20,r:0.05,er:0.005});
---
<Layout title="ETF Cost Calculators and Filings | The Fee Meter Desk" description="See how ETF expense ratios, spreads and dividend withholding change long-term costs. Compare transparent scenarios and read source-linked registration filings."><h1>Small print.<br/>Long-term cost.</h1><p class="lead">An ETF’s expense ratio is only one part of ownership cost. Start with a transparent fee model, add trading costs, then check what the prospectus actually says.</p><p class="note">Models and field guides last updated <time datetime={site.modelsRevised}>{site.modelsRevised}</time> · Filings desk: frozen historical SEC snapshot observed <time datetime={snapshotDate}>{snapshotDate}</time>, not refreshed.</p><div class="desk"><section><h2>Put the fee in perspective.</h2><p>10,000 invested for 20 years, earning an assumed 5% before a 0.50% annual expense ratio. No contributions or taxes.</p><a href="/tools/expense-ratio/">Change the assumptions →</a><p class="note">Illustrative annual model, not a forecast. Actual fund expenses accrue through net asset value.</p></section><aside class="meter"><span>Difference from a zero-fee path</span><strong>{d.totalCost.toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:2})}</strong><p>Including {d.feesPaid.toFixed(2)} in modeled fees and {d.forgoneGrowth.toFixed(2)} in forgone growth. Currency-neutral units.</p></aside></div><section class="tools">{tools.map(([slug,name,q],i)=><div class="tool"><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1} / Model</span><h2><a href={'/tools/'+slug+'/'}>{name} →</a></h2><p>{q}</p></div>)}</section><section><h2>A filing is not a launch.</h2><p>Our EDGAR desk surfaces registration search results, not a list of approved or newly trading funds. Amendments can concern existing products.</p><a href="/filings/">Inspect the filings desk →</a></section></Layout>